Iranian students are prepared to drift for their country's nuclear program.
Created a Human Shield
Hundreds of high-college students created a human shield around a nuclear site in Iran.
Through this gesture, they want to support their country's nuclear programme in the face of a possible Israeli onslaught.
The students started pamphaging at noon in front of the site and then desired the death of the United States and Israel.
A few hundred students from Isfahan's universities created a human shield on Tuesday around Isfahan's nuclear technology center where uranium is transformed.
As a result, they openly expressed that they would defend their country's nuclear agenda at the risk of their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) noted in its most recent report that Iran has continued to strengthen its nuclear weapons.
There are reports in Israel of a possible attack on Iranian non-nuclear facilities.
The students started pamphaging at noon in front of the site and then desired the death of the United States and Israel.
In the event of anattire, the objective of which would be to destroy the Iranian nuclear programme, the targets would not only be Isfahan, but also the Natanz site where uranium is enriched.
