The Run competes all over America.
Revision
Originally a trouble-free race is transformed due to a set of stupid mistakes of people who don't have to do anything in a routine morning trip at work.
To some extent it fulfils everyone's ambition, but it makes no use if no one wants to do anything more.
Subscribing The Run produced great expectations before its release.
He promised to take a new direction with the Older Need for Speed racing series and to release a kind of game from playable games that wouldn't stand only with dots.
So we were curious about the passages added in which the main hero comes out of his car and does what he craves.
As already done in the NFS series, the result is completely different from what was being matched.
These are potentially arcade racing games, but the set is pulling downwards due to a few useless mistakes that have already existed for several years.
These aren't really mistakes, but rather an incomprehensible laziness by developers.
The adventure begins very well.
You're caught in an adventure whose main hero Jack has problems and to fix them starts participating in illegal racing throughout America.
You sit behind the steering wheel on the west coast in San Francisco, and your mission is to arrive first in New York.
The idea has interesting elements.
The itinerary is divided into ten stages and then into more than 50 courses.
As a result, each race takes place on an other route and the stages planned in different environments that differ quite well from each other and are of interest.
The gambler doesn't have the feeling for a single moment that the game offers him something identical.
In addition, some environments are quite beautiful even though the graphic technical level is of the same type as the previous series.
At the same time, this is not the end of the world.
But driving through the desert, in autumn landscapes or in highly snow-covered mountains is very pleasant visually.
The tests are, in addition in good time, adorned with an atypical element.
For example in the desert you end up in a sandstorm that significantly reduces visibility.
Then in the mountains you need to be careful that an avalanche doesn't fall on you.
Aside from this the different races are well arranged one behind each other.
There are only a small number, but that is enough.
There are moments you try to surpass the requested number of adversaries (as in a classic race) then you run against the clock (classic duel with the chronometer) and then still await you another duel with an adversary.
From time to time you also have the font entering the gaming and who are trying to restore the situation.
Novelty is non-velocities.
It's kind of an interactive animation when most of the time Jack runs away in front of someone and you have to help him by typing the right button at the right time.
Nothing complicated.
Surprising is that there are fewer such moments than what you're waiting for (to be concrete there are only three).
As a result, this is the case, because this element does not risk embarrassment and lies, in the context described above, in the elements that adorn the game.
The driving model is in the tradition of previous games.
This means that at the moment there is nothing extraordinary, but it cannot be said that it is negative.
As far as the realistic simap is concerned, you'll have to go somewhere else.
But even though we can find better in concreteness the driving model goes very well with the type of racing design.
So everything is ok.
The problems begin to emerge after a certain period of time.
At the deviation of the driving model, the deviation of collisions is not yet developed.
We don't expect complicated deformity and collision from this game, but when you don't, in a collision with any object, the slightest idea of how your car behaves, so it'sn't completely good.
During tight exceedances you sometimes touch each other lightly but in a different way your car goes into mad flirting.
Or it's crushes.
Thanks to the reboot system it'sn't really a problem, but it really annoys you.
Repeating is done in such a way that when you have broken your face or you have come out in the decor the game takes you back at the moment of the last point on the itinerary.
But you only have five restarts.
When you've used the 5 restarts you have to restart the game from the very beginning.
So it's more of a tool, in case something doesn't go right, whatever something you can really rely on.
Simply the reboots do not help and it is necessary to find the solution by removing from memory the piece of the itinerary in question.
The big problem in this game is that the same actions end up in the same places.
For example, there are certain bends that have to pass in a certain way, otherwise it doesn't happen.
In other words, you encounter "civilian" vehicles in a given location in the same configuration as you arrived first, fifth, 5 seconds in advance or a late minute.
What irritates are the situations when you see the adversary easily pass the adversary between two cars coming in the opposite direction, and when you arrive, you have to either set aside and conturn or slow them down.
It doesn't matter if you go before it because it's "computed" in such a way that for the given situation it always happens very close to your nose.
Opponents have other advantages.
Throughout the time of the game, you arrive in certain places, again without worrying about the weather, and you still have the same adversary that precedes you in the same place.
This energize most at the end of the game when you ride on an onslaught in the opposite direction.
The adversary must at all costs come before you.
When it passes in front of you it hides the view of the other vehicles in the opposite direction and collide a good number of times.
You can understand that the purpose of this game is to do something captivating and full of adredaline, but it's clear you get bored quickly.
And it's a pity, because through a simple driving model the game is interesting, and places with so much action you don't have enough time to track everything that's going on.
And it doesn't matter whether it's because of the concept of 50 single itineraries, that the racing order is such that there's no chance of getting bored or something else.
The original idea is the change of cars during racing.
You have to pay attention to gasoline pumps on the itineraries because you can change cars there most of the time most of the time that you've got you enough.
The cars are divided into three categories.
Sports cars are ideal for cities, large US cylinders for straight motorways and sports super cars with exotic adorns on highly technical pipelines, e.g. on yaw roads in the mountains.
And the mode of challenges, which are racing in particular places that you know about adventure, goes very well with the main diet of history.
Receive not only medals but also experience points that are in addition to your common profile of challenges and adventure.
When you have reached the highest level of conductor, different objects start unlocking:
It connects on-line with the Autolog function which, among other things, compares your results obtained with those of other players and gives you other functions in the community.
One of the most difficult blows to understand is the situation of the last race of the adventure.
You arrive with your car in the metro lanunnel (it resembles) where you ride in the dark on the lanes (it looks like).
Your speedometer tells you between 150 and 200 kilometers per hour (aprendoubtedly) and a melting train arrives behind you that sends the car straight to the scrap.
At the time of writing we had a discussion for a few days about whether anyone actually thought when creating this game or whether the writers really take us for fools.
The technical part of the game isn't expensive, but the visual part is generally pleasant and in some cases really great.
What's disgusting is that in more extreme situations, imagery doesn't hold the level and, in some cases, tragic.
This mainly concerns accidents with a large number of participants when fluid imagery no longer serves any purpose.
The sound part is good and the lad track has a choice.
In an attempt to please as many people as possible, especially the young audience, a new soundtrack has been created in the "I Mix Everything" style, but it can be expected that no one will buy the game for the music.
General Impression of Need for Speed: The Run is therefore really confusing.
If the game didn't have these foolish mistakes we could safely say that this is the best NFS production in recent years.
But this game doesn't give the impression of not being finished.
Amusement is really good, but make every effort to make mistakes flock you in the eye with the strength of an aerodrome reflector.
velvet students in conjunction with the choirs of Charles University
The Festa Academica festival offers festivities for the third time that link International Student's Day with the velvet anniversary with a musical game.
During the course of the festival, 20 choirs from graduating graduate schools and secondary classes occurred.
The highlight of the festival consists of two concerts on 17 November.
'Char Charles University has an important share in this festival.
"Among the choirs are the Chorus of Pedagogicals and Humanities, in the festival committee resels Rector Vaclav Hampl," says the head of the organizing team Jakub Calou.
The highlight of the festival is the concert of Choeur des lychees and secondary classes which takes place with free entry on 17 November from 2 p.m. on the space located in front of the National Technical Library in Dejvice.
In the programme is the composition of the well-known Czech jazzman Karel Ruzicka, Celebration Jazz mass.
During the evening there is the concert "Vlvet students" in the premises of the National House in Vinohrady, during which choirs of the higher schools as well as that of the Charles University perform.
Festa Academica aims not not only to celebrate International Students'Donus Day with dignity and recall the 22nd Anniversary of the velvet revolution, but also to present to the public chorus music at the highest level and develop the creative co-corolment of young people.
The main organizer is the Union of Czech Choirs in cooperation with Lyceum Jan Kepler.
All the action took place under the aegis of Bohuslav Svoboda, Mayor of Prague and Vaclav Hampl, Rector of Charles University.
The festival takes place from 16 to 20 November in Prague and Pardubice.
In addition, the programme features high-level concerts, ms medical encounters, a happening student and other activities.
Stakeholders will be able to find all the information on the Internet pages of the festival www.festaacademica.cz.
Vicenova, Ambassador to the European Union:
The Czechs are behaving like negativizers and Eurosceptians
"The Treaty of Lisbon has radically eliminated the balance between the institutions"
"I didn't expect such a hard-while."
'It will last 5.6 years before the situation calms down and all the players become accustomed to their new role,' this is how Miléna Vicenova began her presentation at the Faculty of Law by the Czech ambassador to the European Union.
When it has succeeded in describing the different bodies of the EU and their relations so comprehensible and visibly, to such an extent that a large number of lecturers at the Faculty of Law of the Charles University could envy it, she has shown to what extent she takes her motto 'undercomprehensible and openly about Europe' very seriously.
Mrs Vicenova paid tribute to the work of Herman Van Rompuye, the new Permanent President of the European Council.
"From the very beginning resonated the critics that it's bland, that it's a bacusses, that it can't fold up any mission and I have to say that it took the breath away from everyone because it derives its role to perfection."
'It is a man who can listen to 27 Member Member States, communicate well with them and has a clear vision of the leadership of Europe.'
She explained the new post of the High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Defence Policy as part of an answer to the question: 'Who is to the European Union?" 'What telephone number should I call?', therefore as an important step towards unity and greater legibility of EU policy vis-à-vis the states, as is China or India.
No one wants to ban our syrecky (cooked dough cheese that smells very loud)
Mrs Vicenova has also mentioned the agenda that the European Council has come to live and will live in a close-term atmosphere.
It described the Czech Presidency as a two-year success.
The Czechs had resolved the rising financial crisis, the gas crisis or had organized an Eastern Partnership Summit.
It described the fall of greed as very negative and damaged the image of the Czech Republic.
The Czech representation in the EU at the moment is very busy at the moment.
In the words of the Ambassador, 'the activity has been in full blur, not only for the Presidency, but also for the financial crisis, which is still coming to an end now.
In addition, we need to approve the Union's new septimal budget, which is becoming very complicated due to the current economic situation.
As it would seem that the budget will be sluggish and with a view to saving, which branch will have the priority, which countries will be helped most, at least, everything has to be resolved in the context of future negotiations.
The Ambassador recalled her slogans with which she arrived in Brussels 'For an comprehensible Europe'.
"I really don't like abbreviations, foreign words, jargon that anyone understands.
As the citizen must understand that it is true that in Brussels no one makes round or twisted gherkins, bananas that are differently large or that no one has prevented us from making syrecky."
It wants to make better use of the EU environment and see more Czechs in the European institutions.
A multi-velocity Europe awaits us
According to the Czech Ambassador have a reputation for being Eurosceptics and people who see things only in their negative aspect more than positively.
In addition, she is sorry to see such a small Czech representation in the European institutions.
In her view, the founivable stemmed from several factors, such as the timidity of our candidates, their inability to write a letter of motivation and weak support from the Czech side.
In addition to a successful Czech presidency, it then stressed the strength and cooperation of the Visegrad Group.
"Believe me, when the Polner, the Magyar, the Slovakia, this Frenchman tells me: 'Hé, what are you doing out there, what does this Visegrad group still do? And it's not at all happy.'
According to Madam Vicenova, in the near future new tough rules on budgetary policy await the Member States.
It is the concept of a two-speed two-speed Europe that prevails rather than a 'New European Federation'.
"We have countries in the euro area and others outside the zone."
"We have the Schengen area, we also have the Institute for Enhanced Cooperation".
In the first place, it has been said that the countries that want them cooperate with each other and those that don't want to remain in their corner."
'There will be a lot of institutes of this kind and there will be a truly two-speed Europe,' Expects Vicenova.
From this point of view, it also appreciated the mission of the Czech Republic and Herman Van Rompuye to determine the basis that all issues with an impact on the EU must be discussed among all members of the EU and not just the euro area.
Story of a brand:
The IBM Innovator Becomes the Second Century
If anyone were to look for the word that expresses the IBM strategy as closely as possible, the closest would be "the long term".
For a large IBM Audience is the symbol of the technological revolution, is a firm felt to be very current and yet since its inception has passed a hundred years.
The basis of this long-term strategy was laid by the firm's first leader, Visionary Thomas J. Watson Sr.
He left that a large number of global problems could be solved if people were willing to think.
Its motivating "PENSE" has become the imprint around which the life of a future giant will develop (and also the title of the internal magazine that IBM began to edit in 1935).
This was the basis of the corporate culture developed by Watson.
For us, IBM means a long-term thinking of continuous movements directed towards the future.
IBM survived a hundred years thanks to the fact that it always remained faithful to its core values and yet was not afraid to change all the others around it.
This has enabled us during our first century to transform technology, business and society.
We hope that in the second century we will reach the current director Samuel J. Palmisano for the birthday.
A well-prepared
In the thirties in the thirties, he began to take care of its employees like Bata in the Czech Republic - IBM people were the only ones among the first American employees to have paid vacation, insurance paid by the employer plus an elegant employee uniform and a well-designed system of rewards for inventories.
