Virtually no one can comprehend what happened, or even the reasons for this war.
According to Peter Englund, "the lack of facts was compounded by assumptions, hopes, fears, fixed ideas, conspiracy theories, dreams, nightmares and rumours."
"Beautiful and sorrow" follows individuals such as Florence Farmborough, an English nannister in the Russian army, as well as Richard Stumpf, a young sailor from the German deep-sea fleet.
Their histories are drawn mainly from memoirs, letters and other documents already published.
