The New Environmental Review commissioned by the Department of State would probably have postponed any decision until 2013, following next year's elections, although civil servants deny political involvement in the decision.
Obama, in a written statement last week, described the decision as the Department of State decision and expressed its support.
The 2,735-kilometer pipeline would extend from Canada to the Gulf of Mexico.
It would transport 700,000 barrels per day from the Province of Alberta to refineries in Texas.
To that end, it would have to travel through six States.
It is hated by ecologists, but loved by working groups, who have bet on the estimated 20,000 jobs related to the pipeline.
But Nebraska gentlemen opposed to this plan lobbied that a strong law will move away from the Sand Hills area and the Ogallala Afquisity, a major source of drinking water and irrigation.
The ongoing environmental impact study of the Department of State found that the project would pose only limited negative environmental impacts, but the energy industry stated that the inspector-General of the Ministry had ordered a separate investigation from the review process, focusing on two issues.
One thing is that a lobbyist hired by Trans-Canada, Paul Elliott, who was Hillary Clinton’s campaign adviser in 2008, would represent a conflict of interest in the program.
The other is whether a company that was hired to conduct the initial study was an inappropriate choice because of its relationship to TransCanada.
Patti LaBelle chased for supposedly causing a young child to vomit with feat
A family in New York claims that diva Disco Patti La-Belle thrown into an unleading of violence in the lobby of their Manhattan building terrified their granddaughter to the point where she vomited with fears.
"Lady Marmalade" studded the 18-month-old Geneviève Monk, to such an extent that she suffered "difference changes, sleep disturbances" and "increased fear of strangers", said her family during the Manhattan Supreme Court lawsuit.
It was on November 10 of last year when stage technician Kevin Monk, his kindergarten bachelor's wife, Roseanna, and Geneviève were getting ready to go on a family trip.
As Kevin Monk went to fetch the car, Roseanna Monk sailed in the lobby of their Riverside Boulevard building with luggage, carrying Geneviève in her arms.
Roseanna Monk stated that she stopped near the gate and placed her daughter for a moment.
"Someone came up behind me and said, 'Do you know what your daughter is doing? I said 'yes' and I went looking for her,'" she said.
LaBelle angrily embellished the pregnant woman angrily.
"She told me in an aggressive tone: 'You shouldn't leave your daughter close to the gate,' said Roseanna Monk.
'I replied: 'what you're saying or thinking doesn't interest me.'
She became enraged and started using swearing - the word "" and the word "" in a loud voice...
She had a bottle of water and started sprinkling water from the bottle.
She stated that at this point, Geneviève became hysterical.
'I said to this woman: 'Look what you did to my daughter,' said the child's mother.
LaBelle threw herself on the mother - who was still holding Geneviève in his arms - and had to be restrained by his entourage who dragged her towards a car that awaited them, says Roseanna Monk.
