Entitlements to contributions to the literature
Books of a social nature contemplified in programmes such as the Rescate de Espacios Publicos and 3x1 migrants may not be finished where serious delays due to the lack of economic resources are found.
The Director of Municipal Social Development had indicated that, although construction programmes had progressed so far, they were in a situation of risk, since the State Government had not fulfilled its obligation to offer contributions of more than 11 million pesos in the three programmes.
He pointed out that the total investment of those three programmes amounted to approximately 50 million pesos, of which the State had to contribute 25 per cent and so far only the Federation and the Municipe had provided resources for the works, so there was the possibility of a delay in their finalization.
'They have to provide a contribution of EUR 12 million and in spite of the fact that the year is about to end they have given us nothing, even if since July they had to give us part of it", he said, 'and we, not to record delays, we have started the works and we have made a lot of progress, but we need the money.'
He pointed out that last year, during the administration of Jesus Aguilar Padilla, the State had not paid the corresponding contributions, therefore at the beginning of the administration Municipe had to request an appropriation to cover the EUR 7 million which the State administration had not provided on that occasion.
'We had already experienced this in the previous sex period because the state had not had the economic capacity to participate and the programmes continue to operate, and this this year, in order to be able to gain access to these programmes, we had to obtain the resources to cover what the state hadn't paid," he said.
Despite the fact that there was a commitment on the part of the State authorities to provide these resources, he stated that they had requested the Secretary of Administration and Finance, Armando Villarreal, to activate the management so that the corresponding percentages would arrive as soon as possible.
'They must contribute almost 12 million and despite the fact that the year is about to come to an end, they didn't give us anything."
Court validates "analog cut-off" in Mexico in 2015
Subscribing an analog signals by fingerprints is one of the most important changes that the world has suffered in recent years
The Supreme Court of Justice of the Nation (SCJN) dismissed the constitutional controversies that the Senat and the Chamber of Deputies formulated against the presidential decree, the so-called 'analog cutting' from 2021 to 2015, because the eight votes needed to invalidate it have not been combined.
A minority of four ministers, hereinafter included the President of the Court, Juan Silva Meza, considered that President Felipe Calderon did not go beyond his responsibilities when he issued the decree detailing the steps to be taken in order to achieve the transition to terrestrial digital television.
With this result, the constitutional controversy promoted by the Senate of the Republic has been rejected for failing to reach a qualified majority of eight votes for the Court to rule on the constitutionality or non-constitutionality of the decree, and this continues to be in force.
The draft sentence, drawn up by Minister Olga Sanchez Cordero, proposed the declaration of the decree as unconstitutional, in view of the fact that the regulations in the field of radio and television are an attribution reserved by law to the Federal Telecommunications Commission (Cofetel), in contravention of the principles of hierarchical subordination and reservation of law.
As part of the project, it voted only for Jorge Mario Pardo, Margarita Luna and Sanchez Cordero.
With this argument, both the Senate and the Chamber of Deputies promoted two constitutional controversies to challenge the decree and by admitting the complaints, Minister Sanchez Cordero has suspended the application of the decree and all the actions planned by it for the digital transition.
The plenary session of the ministers also resolved the complaint made by the Chamber of Deputies, without discussing the project for which Minister Sanchez Cordero was also responsible.
In his speech, the Minister-in-Chief stated that he did not agree with the project's arguments, in the sense that the Federal Execution could not struct through general standards the measures for the public administration.
'I also only consider whether the autonomy of the regulatory body would affect the self-government of the regulatory body, and he pointed out that the planning of public policies in strategic areas such as the telecommunications sector is the responsibility of the Federal Executive, whose constitutional mandate lies with the management of the State.
Subsidising analog signals with digital signals is one of the most important changes that the world has suffered in recent years, and this translates into better exploitation of radio spectrum, better signal quality and more channels.
Deploring change, he argued, would depreciate the benefits of digitalisation, which implies a public-interest decision that not only has a technical dimension, 'because it also includes economic, social, political and national security issues'.
Those questions, he stressed, "requires the operation of an entire system establishing, in accordance with the principle of the economic direction of the State, encompasses a group of responsibilities granted by the Constitution to the power of the Executive of the State".
He pointed out that a large number of countries from all countries had already completed the digital transition and had done so through the Executive, despite the fact that they had highly specialized technical bodies.
It cannot be concluded that the Executive, by issuing the disputed decree, has invaded the sphere of competence of Congress in one form, since it ensures in the administrative sphere compliance with the laws issued by the Legislature, he assumed.
An analysis is made of the possibility of 'drong-drending vote-by-vote' in Michoacon
Depending on the data identified by PREP, the difference between the first and second places in the governor's election is only 27 per cent, even without counting the votes corresponding to the 879 of the 6,000 74 total records.
The possibility of “vote by vote” is a reality with regard to the electoral process this year in Michoacin, where, according to the data highlighted by the Statutural Results Programme (PREP), the difference between the first and second place of the governor's election is only 27 per cent, even without counting the votes corresponding to the 879 of the 6,674 total reports.
In this regard, the President of the General Council of the Electoral Institute of Michoacin (IEM), Maria de los Angeles Llanderal zaragoza, pointed out that a few days a few days ago, the electoral body had approved a series of guidelines for harmonizing local standards to the federal electoral reform.
It will be recalled that Michoacin did not ensert its Political or State Electoral Code or Senate Justice Act, at the same time as the State Congress approved the reforms shortly before the completion of the statutory deadline for this electoral process to come into force, and Governor Leonel Godoy Rangel omitted its publication within the time-limit laid down in the Official Journal of the State.
On 9 November, the Supreme Court of National Court of Justice (SCJN) resolved the constitutional controversy promoted by Local Legislature and described as "invalid and illegal" the vote of the state representative for constitutional reforms, as he does not have the right to "snake or contest them".
Interpreted on the possibility of "drone by vote", Maria de los Angeles Llanderal stated that, thanks to the approval of the corresponding guidelines by the EI General Council, it will be possible to carry out the partial and total counts of votes by the local electoral body.
For example, the partial counting of votes, of one or more electoral bundles, it is possible that: the results of the minutes do not coincide; there are no minutes of the ballots and counting down in the case of urrnator cases are not located in the urrnish president; or there are obvious errors or tarriages of the minutes.
In addition, the total counting of the votes received in all the ballot boxes of the election may be made when there is an indication that the difference between the nominee winning the respective elections and the one who obtained the second place in the ballot is equal to or below a percentage point; provided that at the beginning of the session there is an express petition from the representative of the party and/or coalition who presented the second of the nominees.
The total counting of the vote can also be carried out if, at the end of the co-excise statement, it follows that the difference between the candidate who is supposed to win and that of second place is equal to or less than one percentage point, provided that there is an express petition of the representative of the political party from which the candidate came second, in which the electoral parcel will be excluded which have been the subject of the partial count.
It must be mentioned that this is the situation of Morelia’s election, where, according to the PREP, the difference between first and second place is only 0.16 per cent, even without accounting for 129 of the 923 total records.
