"Going to Costa Rica is a Dreath that Has Become a Reality"
In Exclusive Interview with Viva, bassist Jeff Ament of Pearl Jam said the band is ready to offer one of their best concerts next Sunday at National Stadium.
They waited for more than 20 years, but the group assures that for them it will also become a dream come true to happen in this country.
This is that bassist and founding member Jeff Ament, talking exclusively with Viva of Brazil last week.
The group is in the South American wing of its two-time work-defunct celebration tour and on Sunday 20 will make its only stopover in Central America.
On that day will appear on the National Stadium from 7:30 a.m., next to the Los Angeles Group The X and Las Robertas nationals.
This is an excerpt from the conversation, the complete transcription of which can be found in La Nacion on the Internet.
For its Costa Rican enthusibilities, the fact that Pearl Jam will occur in Costa Rica is a dream come true. Are you aware of what your fans are experiencing?
Moving to Costa Rica is a dream that has become a reality for us too.
This is our second time in South and Central America, and so far it has been magnificent.
I spent the vacation in Costa Rica alone; it is such a beautiful country, and I think we can spend a few days there.
So it emotions us to wear our music there.
I ask you, because there's a kind of devotion to the group, the fans live intensively in the previous days.
What is your message for your most devout adept?
Thank you for standing beside us all these years.
It took us 21 years for us to arrive in Costa Rica; thank you for having waited so long and we are sorry for the fact that so much time had to pass until this concert.
Some people already say that his concert is the biggest show of the year.
