We donated two gigantic shows in Sao Paolo, and we look forward to editing this concert in Costa Rica.
We're really looking forward to doing it.
We love this country, we like to surf and the Jungle; for both things, Costa Rica is one of the best countries in the world.
How did you discover Costa Rica and its surf waves?
We have a lot of surfer friends and I have a very good friend who lives in Tamarindo and the waves are unbelievable there.
My friends were always going to surf in Costa Rica and Nicaragua, beside Mexico, are great places for surfing; that's how we've learned, through people who love surfing.
Looking at the tour, you offered huge shows, with lots of songs.
What did you plan for your presentation in Costa Rica?
Since we have never done ourselves there, we have no restrictions with regard to what we can do.
We will try to make the best show possible, with a wide variety of songs; we will try to perform two songs from each album and offer our fans a good and diverse repertoire.
You don't ever rehears the repertoire.
What does this deserve?
I don't think it's partly because we have nine discs and we can perform more than 120 songs and everyone likes different songs, that's why it's very difficult to choose which songs perform each evening.
When we have two or three songs in the repertoire that we've not performed for a very long time, it helps us to stay focused and surprising because it reminds us of why we love these songs and that we may have forgotten.
This makes the show more interesting for us and therefore I think it's also becoming more attractive to people.
With this tour, you're celebrating 20 years of trajectory.
Looking back, is it hard to believe everything you've achieved?
Yes, absolutely.
First of all, I don't think any of us had imagined that we were going to form a big rock band, and the fact that we did it for more than 20 years makes it seem like a dreason.
We keep recounting our blessings and being able to keep making music together arouses us a great deal.
We love each other and we love creating music.
We are lucky to go to places in the world we've always wanted to go.
Things couldn't do better for us.
What does it mean for you to have been a fundamental element in the creation of grunge?
It has always been an honour for us to form part of this group of major groups.
We're very close friends with people from Soundgarden, Mudhoney and Alice in Chains.
Surprising when a movement emerges from a group of friends and is unconscipated.
From time to time, a bundle emerges from a city, but it's much stranger when five or ten groups come out of the same city at the same time.
We are proud and it is an honour for us to form part of the Seattle group.
We still play with some of them from time to time.
Last year we participated in a festival with Alice in Chains and we were in Canada with Mudhoney, we saw in Soundgarden on their tour, so we're luckily of still being friends with all of them and it's an honour for us to form part of this Seattle sound that has emerged.
It's also very weird that a group like yours will stand united with the same members for so much time.
Yes, four of us have been together for 21 years, and Matt (Cameron) rejoined us 13 years ago, and only that's a lot more time than a lot of groups normally last.
In the first place, I believe that we are all lucky to be still alive and, in the second place, we are all concerned about others.
We're all intimate friends, and thanks to that there are musical boulevards that give everyone the freedom to experiment.
We have confidence in each other with each other's music, and that wouldn't be any better.
It has not been an easy relationship with the celebrity; however, thanks to your success, you've been able to do what you want.
How do you find a balance?
As we grew up, it was easier for us to find a balance.
We make sure that we don't spend too much time on tour because it's easy to fall into this game of big multitudes and people who love your music.
If we don't forget that people are there for music, it doesn't help us not to forget that we need to respect the music and what brought it, without putting in mind the fact that we're famous and a rock-star, which doesn't really interest any of us.
How do you remember your other project, Mother Love Bone?
I don't think we wrote good songs and at the beginning it was great.
We have been a group for almost three years, and we did not release a record until Andy (Andrew Woods died).
There's a lot of frustrations about the fact that it lasted so little and most important is the fact that we're still very close friends with Bruce (Fairweather) and Greg (Gilmore) who started in the band with us and when I listen to a song where I see a picture I'm thinking about the incredible person that Andy was and how he made me cheer, it's always been a pleasure.
He was an astonishing human being and we miss him.
The national group Las Robertas will open the show in Costa Rica.
It's true that you know his work, especially Eddie Veddder?
Yes, the production sent us videos with different proposals and this one was the group that we liked the most, so we can't wait to see what Las Robertas can offer live and it must be very entertaining.
What do you always change Yello Ledbetter lyrics live?
This is a question for Ed (Eddie Vedder), so I don't know.
It is he who sings it and I believe that he does so with the first words he imagines.
As a bass player, what are its influences?
There are so many...
Geezer Butler, John Entwistle, C. J. Ramone, John Doe, Paul McCartney, Chuck Dukowski
There are so many influences, that I could talk all afternoon about the bassists that I love.
How did Pearl Jam keep grunge undercover despite the fact that it is no longer bushed?
I don't think we all feel a little disconnected from the word grunge.
When I think of it, it reminds me of the bands I just mentioned, like Mudhoney, Soundgarden, Nirvana and all those that came out at the same time and, if this is relevant now, I think it's marvellous, because it's music worth listening and bands like Mudhoney are now making the best music than ever.
At the beginning, his music had a more obscure content and now it became more positive.
What is the need for this change?
It's interesting, because I don't think there are songs in the new album that seem lighter, but there are also songs, like The End or "Just Breathe" described as very obscure songs, even though they may sound a little positive.
With both, when Ed played them for me, I cried when I listened to them, and these are deeply obscure songs.
I don't think that if you grow up and there's a trauma in your life and you lose to a relative or friend, these things start to influence your art and your music and these songs, no doubt, represent this to me.
I also think we can also be happily, and you can do dark music.
Peru:
Fujimori re-housing for medical examinations
Former President Alberto Fujimori was hospitalized on Tuesday in a public hospital to be evaluated for the loss of muscular strength he presents in the magpies, informed his family doctor.
Fujimori, a 72-year-old Fujimori who is serving a 25-year prison sentence for human rights violations committed during his Government (1990–2000) suffers from a variety of ailments, which include language cancer for which he was operated on four times and is under supervision.
Congresswoman Alejandro Aguinaga, his personal doctor, stated for Channel N television that Fujimori will be evaluated for three days at the National Institute of Neoplasic Diseases to determine the reason for the pain and the loss of strength in its lower members.
Aguinaga commented that Fujimori in its opinion would be a candidate to obtain the benefit of the surrender of the sentence for humanitarian reasons, no doubt, he said he did not want it because he feels innocent.
It was operated on four times with tongue cancer, it had a weight loss of 18 kg, and other pathologies, such as severe erosive gastritis, pancreas cyst, kidney stones, high blood pressure and circulation problems in the feet, enumerated the doctor.
Fujimori has been practicing imprisonment since September 2007 in the National Police Enforcement Directorate.
In April 2009, he was sentenced to 25 years'imprisonment for the death of 25 people because of an annihilation squad of the army that operated clandestinely during the first years of his government.
Mujica travels to Mexico to strengthen political ties
An official procession, headed by the Uruguayan President, José Mujica, of various ministers and boss, will begin on Tuesday a visit to Mexico to expand trade between the two nations and address political issues in the region.
Mujica will meet next Wednesday with its Mexican counterpart, Felipe Calderon, the highest point of a long agenda of meetings with the political and commercial authorities and a meeting with the community of Uruguay residents in Mexico, according to the agenda circulated by the Uruguayan Presidency.
The meeting between the two presidents in Guadalajara, will be 'promoting for the exchange of information in political affairs between the two nations', according to the information published by the Presidency of the South American country on its web page.
According to local media reports, Mujica is trying to convince Calderon to support Uruguay in the incident with France that took place when the French practitioner, Nicolas Sarkozy, included the South American country on the list of tax havens, in the G20 meeting in the French city of Cannes.
In his speech, Sarkozy threatened to exclude from the international community the countries which continue to be tax havens, a declaration which provoked the rejection of Uruguay and the call for consultations of its ambassador from that European country.
Since November, Mexico has premeditated the G20, a group made up of the world’s leading emerging and developed countries, with the South American country since January this year, an agreement to exchange fiscal information to avoid double taxation.
The Uruguayan Government has tried in recent years to launch the implementation of tax-exchange agreements in order to break out of the 'grai list' of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), integrated by countries which do not implement all international standards of cooperation in tax matters.
At the commercial level, Mexico and Uruguay have been in force since 2004 a Free Trade Treaty (TLC), which has increased the exchange of goods between the two nations.
The moustached plumber switches to three-storey with "Super Mario 3D Land"
Super Mario wrestled, indefatigable, for 25 years to save Princess Peach the clutches of navy Bowser, but he had never done it in three dimensions: in "Super Mario 3D Land" he will compete for the young girl's love in stereoscopic technology.
The title, which arrives this month at everyone's stores, was designed from the beginning to make good use of the features of the Nintendo 3DS mobile console, which allows three-dimensional play without using glasses.
"Mario is the character who has to properly functional stereoscopy without glasses," said Nintendo Special Press Officer Omar Alvarez during the presentation of the Video Game in Madrid.
Alvarez stated that "Super Mario 3D Land" is "the first Nintendo Video Game originally designed for this medium," because until now successes such as "Star Fox 64 3D" or "Selda: Ocarine of time 3D" were adaptations of existing titles.
Nintendo Spokeswoman argued that, despite being in 3D, "Super Mario 3D Land" is an "accessible" video game that allows a fast and fluid game.
Alvarez claimed that "Super Mario 3D Land" contains two games in one: the first part is "simple" to hook less clever users.
Once surmounted, the most pundits will be able to do a "second round" at game levels, which this time are more difficult.
In addition, users will be able to choose in real-Type between an "aggratile D" or one which only affects the depth of the action, but it would be necessary to play in three dimensions in order to be able to overcome the various challenges and 'do not succumb to optical illusions'.
This incursion of Super Mario into all three dimensions also presupposes the return of the character to a mobile console, which has not happened since 2005.
In Nintendo Video Gambling a nozzle to saga enthusiasts and repeats the success formula of previous games, which consists in the fact that the musted plumber must browse through perimeter-matter platforms to free Princess Peach.
Even if I find novelties in movements, environments, costumes and enemies and also in "playable" Luigi cases.
Colom adorns Portillo's extradition in the United States
President 'lvaro Colom announced last Tuesday that he had issued an order for the extradition of former Governor Alfonso Portillo to respond to the United States for the 70-million-dolgrance United States-dollar Laundering Conspiracy.
This concludes the trial in order to respond to the request of the country of the north, which was calling for Portillo to try it.
At a press conference, Colom stated that its decision was based on the independence of the judiciary and the judiciary, taking into account that a court of first Instance had already ordered his extradition.
He stated that during his term of office "he did not assist" in any judicial resolution, and he gave effect to all the extraditions he had experienced.
Apart from Portillo, Sergio Ruano Marroquon would also be extradited for murder and serious injuries, and Edgar Estrada Morales and Vector Estrada Paredes would be extradited for drug trafficking.
What Colom has done presupposes an executive approach after exhausting all judicial and constitutional bodies to judge the former proxy of the 2004-2004 period.
According to the resolutions of the Fifth Criminal Tribunal and the Constitutional Court (CC), Portillo should be extradited after resolving its legal situation in Guatemala and after guaranteeing its human rights.
Portillo was absolute for embezzlement of Q120 million to the Ministry of Defence when he was president, which was the pre-executive trial, but the Public Prosecutor's Office appealed and reactivated the case.
Trinijove helped 6,000 young people at risk
The entity was born in order to avoid the marginalization of untrained young people
The assessment of the first 25 years of life of the social support entity Trinijove is important: 6,000 young people at risk of exclusion have received help to overcome a difficult situation during this quarter of a century.
Added to this is the long centennial of jobs currently obtained by this social group.
The birthday served yesterday to take stock in an act celebrated in a former Fabra i Coats Industrial Complex in which more than 300 people attended.
Trinijove was born in Trinitat Vella in 1986 with the aim of helping people who are poorly trained, without any work, with problems of drug addiction or marginalization.
The celebration of yesterday in Sant Andreu concentrated a large number of officials of entities and institutions who in those 25 years collaborated with the association.
The varied political representation in the middle of an electoral season has shown the unitary nature of Trinijove’s work.
Behind the Catalan (Generalitat), Artur Mas and its predecessor Jordi Pujol, attended the act former Minister of Socialist Education, Ernest Maragall and former Deputy Mayor to Mayor Ricard Goma.
The current Minister of Social and Family Well-Befulness, Josep Lluas Cleries and the Director-General of Caixa Charity, Jaume Lanaspa, was also attended in the Grand Hall of Fabra i Coats.
Mas stated that Trinijove was born in a very difficult time and the current one, but he added that the work carried out so far "is a good basis".
The president gave Trinijove as an an example to combat bad circumstances and to give hope to people in difficulty.
'The crisis isn't something new for the entity and the work it does,' he said.
Property invaded by squatters for micro-beests, evacuated
Intrusers had appropriated 11 of the building's 13 apartments in Balmes.
The 12 occupiers abandoned the property at noon yesterday without any resistance
Everything seemed to indicate that the nightmare that the residents of Rue Balmes No. 51 lived had come to an end had come to an end.
Twelve people volunteered at no noon the building that they occupied illegally at noon yesterday and where they were organizing despising micro-festivities that despaired by the neighbours, by judicial order and without the need for action by the police.
At the end of the operation, the door latch was changed in order to prevent a repetition of the situation.
'Since today there will be an access control,' said the trustee.
The squatters, which had invaded 11 of the 13 apartments of the edifice - the rest were inhabited - carried away the electrical installation and part of the water, apart from painting the walls and leaving residues of all kinds, especially the dottes of alcoholic beverages.
The first three apartments were the mass festivities scene, which lasted up to two-day days and despised the tenants.
Behind the edifice there is a discotheque, Balmes 51, which has also been affected.
Its landlord Maria Pantinat explained for Europa Press that as soon as the edifice was occupied, her business dropped an 80 per cent.
The owner of discotheque mentioned that property invaders made it uncompromising competence, because they were selling glasses for three euros, while in the discotheque they were worth 10.
In addition, the owner of the recreation area had had to respond to complaints from the neighbours for the noise, while, according to her, the troubles were not provoked by customers of the discotheque, but by the inhabitants of the occupied house and, above all, the participants at the festivities organized there, who were more frequent and intense in recent weeks, according to irritated neighbours in the area.
The person in charge of the discotheque explained that the trouble was so great that it even reached an agreement with the owner of the building and it has been nine months since he "forgives" the rent.
Guardia Urbana (Municipal Police) also confirmed that in recent weeks they had received more complaints from the neighbours about this situation.
Last week, the chairman of the Mayor's PP municipal group, Alberto Fernandez Daaz, had requested "imimmediate evacuation of the building to end with the problems of life in common and gentlemanism caused to the residents and the degradation of the area".
The popular ruler explained that before the summer only one storefloor of the edifice was occupied, but in the last few months the squatter had occupied all floors of the edifice and almost all the apartments and that in some apartments there had also been flights.
It is in this sense that he added that 'impositivity must be endless and implacable against the anti-social behaviour generated on property.'
Also yesterday, the Mossos (Catalan local police) vacated an edifice at Nou Barris.
At 3:30 a.m., the police moved to Rue Mont-ral No. 35, after receiving a call from a neighbour who had observed that four persons were entering the edifice.
The four were arrested immediately.
Parc or mountain?
Investigators co-conceived the adjunct adjunct of summons over the controversy over fees
The Municipal Contest on 16 Doors again opens debate on Collserola's role in Barcelona
In the mid-1980s, in the midst of the unextinguished Metropolitan Corporation of Barcelona (CMB), this Administration printed posters promoting Collserola.
The pamphlet defined the hike as the great park of Metropolitan Barcelona.
In addition, it also contained a numerical comparison with the Central Park in New York.
With the death of the CMB, in 1987, the park became again, in the imagination of many people, the upper limit of Barcelona, the Catalan capital being the only one that does not orient itself on the north-south axis, if not high (mountain) - bottom (sea).
Collserola qualification as a natural park is to the advantage of this idea.
The reference was no longer Central Park but Yellowstone, with boars in the Yogi Bear.
This was the situation until, in September, the town hall convened a mega-competition composed of 16 competitions for all access doors to Collserola.
A gambby restores the idea of a park, without a doubt.
That's it, or someone wants to put gates in the field.
The question comes up alone: Collserola: park or mountain?
Contest, both as far as its organisation is concerned as far as the reflection on the city is concerned, is a controversial theme for all the architects in Barcelona.
It's almost a recurring theme of which two members of this former caste of eldest people talk when they recognize themselves in an elevator.
And this is precisely one of the few opinions on which three architects from Barcelona, university professors, who have presented themselves, coincide.
Miguel Roldon, Daniel Modol and Marta Bayona: Contest is timely.
According to Roldon, after embarking on the coastal front "it is necessary to" debate on 'mountain front' because Ildefons Cerda's speech, that of green blocks has not been brought to an end.
'It has to start from the base that the wider park of Barcelona is the beach.
Among other things for its great accessibility.
Collserola is more complex", gave the verdict the archectron for whom the title of 'doors of Collserola' contains an "lexicon trap": we should not think of them 'like access to a park, but the demarcation of certain areas in which one has to act'.
Modol, like Roldon and Bayona with experience in the urban planning world, called the proposition "intellectual challenge" with "some perils".
Pervasives that drifted from the "uncertainty of the projection of the public space" after the experiment in the '80s and which occurred in the Forum area "his stove song".
The first feat is the delimitation of the boundaries on which one can build.
'Limiting something means already establishing the next pitch", i.e. its overshoot.
'We need to think about new urban planning and planning instruments, because the current [recommendating the Metropolitan General Plan (PGM) - can cause genuine disasters".
By sticking more to the question, Modol opine than, by simplifying, the slope of the El Valles de Collserola region "may be understood as a park, the park of Barcelona, no".
Modol reminds us that there is already a work done by the Patronat de Collserola which "must not be lost", thanking for the opportunity that the mayor offers to his corporation to intervene in this project 'from the first moment'.
In addition, it understands that the proximity of the mountain to the city is the safe conduct for the architects to enter into the debate, but 'grey' if this technical profile should lead the m multidisciplinary teams ("every success," he says) that we had to create: 'We, the architects, should only be an instrument'.
Bayona insinuates that the answer to the question that gives the title of this piece is complex, because from the bases of the competition it lacks a global vision of Collserola: . . . 16 cross-disciplinary competitions have been summoned - he says - in the mountain-sea direction, but there is not a longitudinal reading that sees and understands the area as a whole".
At least in this case, it has chosen to participate in all 16 competitive examinations.
In some other way, a project so that one of the gates could be shocked in the programme and defined with that of the architect of the nearby gate.
In its opinion, yes, the town hall should guarantee that the band immediately above that of Ronda de Dalt should provide, throughout its extension, for an area of equipment that carries out a gentle transition between the city and the green.
Casino Forgivates Jon's Larrazobal and he will be released
After a 72-day provisional arrest, Casino Red's legal proxy forgiveness to the mayor of Monterrey's wrangler for the trial initiated against him for so-called blackmail
After spending a 72-year-old arrest, Manuel Jon's Larrazabal will be re-disposed after the Legal Power of Casino Red grants him a forgiveness before the Second Criminal Court of the District, which follows a trial for blackmail against the mayor of the mayor of Monterrey.
In the aftermath of the Casino Royale attack, the owner of the Red Casino, Sergio Gil Garcia, published a series of photographs and videos, in which Manuel Jonas supposedly required him to pay for an economic criterion so that the mayor of Monterrey would permit the clandestine operation of the gaming house.
Following public denunciation, the Public Prosecutor opened a criminal trial against the mayor of the Pandicalist mayor, and on 2 September he was Arrested for 30 days.
After four hours in front of the Agent of the Public Public Ministry 3 of Patrimonals, he was transferred to the Detention Centre 1, located in Elder Quarter of the State's capital.
He stayed there for the next 49 days when he was given a second order of detention after the Public Prosecutor's office dismissed the offences of corruption and organized crime.
On the 19th of October he was transferred to Cadereyta Criminal Centre allegedly for blackmailing the owners of Casino Red with one and a half million pesos; but he spent only a few hours in the mid-security detention centre because there were death threats against him.
The authorities enabled him to continue the trial in the Municipal Cells of San Nicholas de los Garza.
On 25 October a capture order was issued by the Clerk of the Second District Penal Tribunal, Jorge Yanez, who stated that after almost two months of investigation there was sufficient confirmed evidence to determine the culprits of Jonas, such as that relating to the collection of 1.5 million pesos from the representatives of the gambling company in exchange for its operation.
On this Monday, Red Casino Legal Scholar, Victor Aldo Garcia Gomez, appeared before Judge José Luis Pecina to seek forgiveness for the brother of the local mayor; he could therefore regain his freedom over the next few hours.
During the legal formalities, the public prosecutor attached to the Tribunal, Ramiro Arias, questioned Garcia Gomez whether the damage had been recovered and who the partners in the gaming house had been the one who had granted forgiveness, but the lawyer tried not to dissipate the name.
Legal forgiveness in Case 19/7/2011 was granted legal forgiveness and no claim could subsequently be submitted concerning the lawsuit brought against him; no compensation for the damage, nor any punishment.
After the hearing of the Legal Power Felence of the Playhouse at 3:50 p.m. Larrazabal Breton's impervious freedom was commanded.
The clerk of the Pretty Court, Jorge Yunez, travelled as far as the prison of the municipe de San Nicholas de los Garza to communicate to Jonas that he had been legally forgiven and his file would be closed.
It will also provide him or her with an immediate order of liberty issued by the judge.
Secretary Dionisio Pérez Jocome provides the details of the air accident in which Government Secretary Francisco Blake has lost his or her life, Francisco Blake
The Communications and Transportation Secretariat (SCT) reported that the results revealed on the accident in which the Secretary of Government, Francisco Blake Mora and others, had lost his life, indicated that the helicopter directly shocked the ground in complete structural integrity, without the pilot being able to attempt a forced landing.
During a press-conference, Dionisio Pérez, Secretary of Communications and Transport, mentioned that prior to take-off of the aircraft, the pilot noted that climate conditions were adequate to fly.
'Excise elements which seem to indicate that the unit had various contacts with the ground, the blades came into contact with the shafts at 25 meters where the unit lost the fuselage."
It was also aware of the fact that the unit was designed for 19 persons, so it met the necessary requirements to transport staff.
In addition, he said that investigations carried out in the impact zone did not indicate the appearance of parts on the ground.
'In one research it was reported that there are no parts or components of the aircraft in another location, the impact showed up in a structural way.
"The helicopter had been designed for 19 passengers and met the requirements to carry them.
The soil had a pante of seven to 30 degrees of inclination.
For the time being, the clerk had assured that a priority was to have the results as soon as possible; but the investigation could last for a few months, it could even last for one year.
In his turn, Gilberto Lopez Meyer, Director-General of Airport and Auxiliary Services, ensured that the moment of the impact, the Chief Regionally Helicopter was running at a competitive speed, and this happened on a moving ascending ground.
'This information supports the hypothesis of normal cruising functioning at the time of impact,' he says.
During the press conference, SCT registrar, Pérez J-come, listed six important elements in the investigation:
Visual hoses:
According to aeronautical standards, the flight was carried out according to the rules of visual flight, which implies that the crew must have visibility during the flight and on the ground.
meteorological conditions:
Reports in the AICM contained adequate take-off conditions, and as the aircraft moved towards the border area between DF and the State of Mexico there were layers of cloud cover at a low height.
Screwed routes:
It is probable that, due to the bulosity conditions, the crew sought an area of lower height and greater visibility towards the Cuernavaca Valley.
Location of impact.
Coordinates of the impact and the last recording of the aircraft on the radar coincide, probably before the impact there was no loss of control or alteration of the flight trajectory.
Dispersion of the residues of the aircraft in a reduced zone:
The information available so far makes it possible to assume that the impact has taken place on a straight and lateral trajectory.
The model for dispersing the remnants of the aircraft makes it possible to assume that the helicopter has collided against the ground under conditions of structural integrity.
Traces of fire or explosion have not been detected:
In the site of the disaster there is still no trace in the remains of the aircraft of an explosion or fire type.
The final results of the investigation indicate that the aircraft had had multiple contacts with the ground.
During the field work, parts of the aircraft amounted to a height of 9,1000,200 feet above the average level of the sea, the ground had a slope from seven degrees to 30 degrees of inclination.
The photographs show the sequence in which it was possibly disarticulated along its path.
The information provides elements that seem to indicate that the helicopter may have had multiple impacts on the ground.
After the meticulous quarrel in an area greater than the encircled place around the accident, dispersing parts of the aircraft were not found, which bears the presumption that the impact took place under conditions of structural integrity.
MSS Announces the Obesesitity Gene for Obsessive Obesity Gene
Social insurance is conducting an investigation to uncover the obesity gene in the case of children and young people; this is supported by NPI specialists
The Mexica Social Insurance Institute (IMSS) has announced that it is directing an investigation to unravel the gene of obesity in the case of children and young people, called 'Obesity Genetics from Children and Adolescents' protocol, which will make it possible to have the markers associated with overstroke.
In a press release, the Head of the Medicated Biochemistry Investigation Unit of the 20th-century National Medical Centre of the National Medical Centre of the 20th Century explained that a multidisciplinary team of doctors, nurses, nutritionists and social workers had been trained.
This team is supported by specialists and graduate students from the National Institute of Public Health (INSP) and the Advanced Investigation and Investigation and Study Centre (Cinvestav) of the National Polytechnic Institute (IPN).
In the investigation, it is called upon to take part in the eligible or non-executed population to come to the participating sports units of the IMSS in Valle de México, where the evidence is carried out every Saturday from 8 a.m. from 8 a.m.
He pointed out that the protocol has started in the Cuauhtémoc Sports Unit (Estado de México Poniente) and that as of 8 October, the activity takes place in the Sporting Unit of Nezahualc-yolt (Estado de México Oriente).
After achieving the goal of bringing together 500 or 600 miners, the study will continue in the Independencia Sports Unit (southern Distrito Federal) and finally the Morelos Sports Unit (north of Distrito Federal).
He explained that the objective of the investigation was to identify the components and the importance of genetics for the development of obessive obesity and to identify risk factors for preventing the occurrence of chronic degenerative diseases.
With 14 November commemorating the World Diabetes Day, he mentioned that the objective is to reunite three thousand children and young people between the ages of 6 and 14, with the consent and under the supervision of their parents, for the implementation of specific food-related questionnaires.
They will also be asked about their physical activity and a history of family inheritance of their diseases, to avoid risk factors that trigger conditions such as diabetes or renal indebility.
He detailed that Saturdays will be applied to all participants anthropometric measurements (weight, pruning waist), blood pressure, determining glucose levels, triglycerides, cholesterol and insulin and genetics (to identify people associated with childhood obedience).
He pointed out that this investigation is the result of the concern of healthcare professionals for the alarming weight gain in the case of minors.
'The health surveys for 1999 and 2006 indicated that in only six years there has been an increase, in the case of 16 per cent, in the case of boys, and in the case of 4 per cent overweight, there has also been a dramatic upward trend in the case of boys in the case of boys.
He pointed out that the justification for tracing markers is based on the fact that the population of the country is different from the others in its genetic history.
He reported that, on an average, Mexicans have an Indo-American heredity of 65 per cent, one 30 per cent European and one five per cent African, and this condition is reflected in people associated with diabetes and overweight.
He explained that, in general, obessive obesity genetics is unable to rust the excessive energy that is consumed (calories), which is deposited in the form of fat.
The researcher explained that the direct benefit to the participants is the full assessment of children, which makes it possible to detect whether they are overweight or obessive.
Ila even says that the presence of dark-colored folds (acanthosis) on the neck and forearm indicates the probability of experiencing metabolic and even pre-diabetic alterations.
The information is managed in a confidential manner, doctors hand it out in a written word to the parents, to whom each of the measures and changes in the lifestyle that they have to carry out in order to prevent the disease is explained.
He explained that there are three main components that cause overstrency, obesity and other chronic conditions: sedentarism, which is the lack of daily physical activity, staying most of the day seated in front of the TV and using means of transport instead of walking on short distances.
Another cause is high caloric intake, i.e. the greatest consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages, carbobohydrates (tamsals - corn-meavolved with corn flour in corn lethal -, bread, pizza, hamburgers, etc.) with a high content of fats and proteins and the genetics analyzed in this protocol.
UNAM asphalt would prevent blackcurrant
Rafael Herrera, a researcher at UNAM Faculty of Chemismia, develops asphalts modified with polymers to produce a mixture with a better yield, regardless of environmental and temperature conditions.
If the reports that the pavement were resolved, it would no longer be necessary to repair about 200 thousand blackstups each rainy season in the Metropolitan Area of Metropolitan of México, warned Rafael Herrera Najera, a researcher of the Faculty of Chemistry (FQ) of UNAM, who ensured that if the process of constructing and maintaining the bitubrothine baving could even be eliminated.
During his Count Technology Opinion, organized as part of the International Chemistry Year, he announced that the lab for which he is responsible develops asphalts modified with polymers to produce a mixture having characteristics similar to that of asphalt, but with greater mechanical strength, both at high and low-temperature.
Herrera suggested that this type of modified asphalt could be used in places where the climate is extremely hot, such as certain cities in the north of the country, to improve efficiency, and therefore the formation of blackcurrants.
He explained that asphalt, the heavier part of oil, is a set of hydrocarbon molecules, molecule with a heavier molecular weight, called asphaltnes, and molecules with a low molecular weight, called malrenes, that together give the pavement its viscoelastic behavior characteristic.
The visco-elastic behaviour of aspphalt consists in the fact that at high temperatures of almost 180 degrees, it behaves like a liquid, at 120 degrees its viscosity is very high, and at 50 degrees It has an almost solid state, while at very low temperatures the asphalt becomes brittle, he added.
This means that the asphalt resistance on the streets is not uniform and changes during the day depending on the environmental and temperature conditions, warns the chemical engineering specialist.
The FQ researcher observed that the streets of Ciudad de México in their majority were covered by a flexible paving, composed of six layers of materials, the last three of which involve asphalt.
Between more superficial layers is the asphalt layer, formed by small asphalta-burned stones and subsequently compacted.
Each of the little stones that form the diaplash, signalled, is bathed an asphalt.
When the vehicles pass there by generating efforts, it allows the forces to propagate very well in the paving stone.
If modified asphalt would propagate the chemical asphalt better.
On the asphalt coat, he says, a last coat called treasure layer, made of fine stone, i.e. s sand which is also bathed into asphalt.
Since this is the layer in contact with the wheels of the vehicles, it must have more mechanical force than the asphalt layer and provide adhesion in the street.
Being the part of the bulwark that receives and distributes the forces, the tread layer also requires that the latter have an adequate thickness and the material of which it is made must be treated.
Climate, especially humidity and changes in temperature, are also a very important factor to be considered, especially water, he says, as they considerably affect the yield of the asphalt layer.
When the soil gets wet, the water spreads inside the diaper is it difficult for it to come out, which softens all the layers of the pavement and consequently causes blackcurring.
In the blackcurrant training process, he said, the first one that was spoiled was the rolling film, and only the asphalt layer was subsequently affected, but the damage did not take place immediately, but it was a process that had to be treated at the first signs with adequate maintenance programmes.
The member of the National Research System explained that vehicle loading is another important factor for blackcurrant formation and therefore the thickness of each cobblestone layer must always be related to the load of vehicles and ensure its satisfaction, in order to avoid frequent blackcurrant training.
Rafael Herrera warned that there is still a lot to investigate and work on asphalt, for example bituminous emulsesions, which in other countries already exist on the market and allow blackcurrant to be repaired easily and without having to use high temperatures.
What did Valle's candidate fail to be the new Miss Colombia?
Analysis of the Factors which caused Melina Ramarez Serna not to obtain the wreath wrangling of Miss Colombia.
Valle received its title number 14 from a princess.
Again Valle del Cauca stayed with the desire to win the crown of Miss Colombia.
